  ('growing-something-green', 210, 'Replant a divided perennial clump at the same depth it was growing before, and water it well.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 211, 'Prune a leggy pothos vine back to just above a node, and root the pieces you cut off.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 212, 'Use clean, sharp scissors or pruners when you trim a plant, so the cuts heal cleanly.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 213, 'Trim a woody herb like thyme or sage lightly after it flowers, never cutting into bare old wood.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 214, 'Gather up fallen petals or leaves from under your houseplants and add them to compost.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 215, 'Notice how a plant''s growth slows in the shorter days of fall and adjust your watering to match.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 216, 'Write a short thank-you in your plant journal to a plant that gave you herbs or flowers this year.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 217, 'Look at a plant that''s struggling and change one thing only, such as its light, its water or its pot.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 218, 'Accept that some plants simply don''t suit your space, and pass them on to someone with a better spot.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 219, 'Visit a greenhouse or conservatory on a cold winter day and spend a few minutes in the warm, green air.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 220, 'Choose a plant for your office desk that copes with fluorescent light, such as a pothos or a ZZ plant.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 221, 'Leave a small watering can or a cup by your desk plant so checking it becomes part of your lunch break.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 222, 'Ask a coworker to check your desk plant''s soil while you''re away, with a note on how much to give it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 223, 'Read your plant''s leaves: yellow and soft often means too much water, crisp and brown often means too little.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 224, 'Let tap water sit in an open jug overnight before watering a sensitive plant like a spider plant or a calathea.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 225, 'Learn the difference between a node and the stem between nodes on one of your plants by finding them with your finger.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 226, 'Find the aerial roots on a pothos or monstera stem, the little bumps where new roots can start.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 227, 'Give a climbing plant a moss pole or a small trellis to grow up, tying the stem on loosely.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 228, 'Pinch off flower buds on basil as soon as you see them, so the plant keeps making leaves.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 229, 'Cut back a mint plant by a third when it gets leggy, and use the trimmings in a drink or a meal.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 230, 'Plant mint in its own pot rather than in a bed, so its runners don''t take over.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 231, 'Grow parsley in a deep pot, since it sends down a long root.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 232, 'Sow cilantro in a pot every few weeks in cool weather, since each sowing goes to flower fairly quickly.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 233, 'Snip rosemary sprigs from the tips of the stems and roast them with potatoes or vegetables.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 234, 'Dry a bundle of oregano or thyme by hanging it upside down somewhere airy and out of the sun.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 235, 'Taste the difference between a leaf from the top of a basil plant and one from lower down.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 236, 'Learn the botanical name of one houseplant, say it aloud, and write it on the pot''s label.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 237, 'Use a plant identification guide or app on a plant at a park, just to learn its name, never to eat it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 238, 'Leave wild plants, berries and mushrooms uneaten unless you are completely certain what they are, and it is simpler still to skip them.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 239, 'Check whether a lily, a sago palm or a dieffenbachia is in your home if you have cats or dogs, since these can harm them.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 240, 'Set toxic houseplants up high or in a room your pets and small children don''t go into.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 241, 'Teach a child to wash their hands after touching potting soil, and help them plant one bean seed in a cup.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 242, 'Grow a bean in a clear jar against a damp paper towel with a child, so you can both watch the roots.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 243, 'Offer to help water the plants at a school or library garden over a vacation break.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 244, 'Bring a cutting or a seed packet to a friend who has just moved into a new home.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 245, 'Sit with a cup of tea beside your plants this evening and look at each one for a few breaths.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 246, 'Run your fingertip softly along a fuzzy leaf, such as a sage or an African violet, and notice its texture.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 247, 'Notice the color of the newest leaf on a plant and compare it with the older ones around it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 248, 'Look for the tiny curled tip of a fern frond unrolling, and check on it again in a few days.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 249, 'Breathe in the smell of damp potting mix the next time you water, and take a slow breath out.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 250, 'Write three words in your plant journal describing how a plant looks this morning.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 251, 'Draw the outline of your favorite houseplant''s silhouette against a bright window.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 252, 'Press a fallen leaf from one of your plants in a heavy book, and tape it into your journal later.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 253, 'Make a simple watering chart for your plants, listing each one and how dry it likes to get.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 254, 'Group plants with similar water needs together, so a watering round is quicker and easier.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 255, 'Put a cactus or succulent in your sunniest window and keep thirstier plants a little farther back.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 256, 'Choose a terracotta pot for a plant that likes to dry out, since clay lets moisture escape.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 257, 'Pick a plastic or glazed pot for a plant that likes steady moisture, such as a fern.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 258, 'Soak a new terracotta pot in water for an hour before planting in it, so it doesn''t pull water from fresh soil.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 259, 'Scrub the white crust off the rim of an old clay pot with a stiff brush and a splash of vinegar.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 260, 'Flush a houseplant''s soil by running plenty of water through it in the sink, letting it drain fully.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 261, 'Top-dress a houseplant by scraping off the top half inch of old soil and adding fresh potting mix.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 262, 'Repot a plant in spring or early summer, when it is growing and recovers quickly.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 263, 'Insist on a pot with a drainage hole for every new plant, even if you hide it inside a prettier one.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 264, 'Cover a large drainage hole with a scrap of mesh or a coffee filter so soil doesn''t wash out.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 265, 'Skip the layer of gravel at the bottom of a pot, and fill it all with potting mix instead.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 266, 'Set a large pot on a plant stand with wheels before filling it, so it is easy to move later.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 267, 'Describe your window to a nursery worker and ask them to help you choose a plant for that exact light.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 268, 'Buy one small, healthy-looking plant with firm leaves, checking under them for bugs before you pay.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 269, 'Take a walk through a nursery''s houseplant section and notice which plants you''re drawn to.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 270, 'Visit a botanical garden''s herb or vegetable beds and look for one plant you''ve never seen growing.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 271, 'Read the signs in a public garden and learn the name of one tree or shrub you pass often.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 272, 'Ask a staff member or volunteer at a public garden what they''re planting this season.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 273, 'Notice one plant you pass every day on your street and look up what it is.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 274, 'Collect a few seeds from a friend''s flowers, with permission, and sow them in a pot.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 275, 'Grow an avocado pit by suspending it over water with toothpicks, broad end down.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 276, 'Plant the top of a pineapple: twist off the leafy crown, let it dry for a day or two, then root it in water.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 277, 'Plant a few seeds from a lemon or an orange in a pot just for fun, keeping them warm and moist.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 278, 'Regrow romaine lettuce from its base in a shallow dish of water, changing the water often.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 279, 'Snip the new leaves from your regrowing green onions and add them to eggs, soup or rice.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 280, 'Give a slow-growing plant a little patience: write down one sign that it is alive and well.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 281, 'Pick up a fallen leaf from a houseplant and look at its stem end to see where it let go.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 282, 'Mist a fern or calathea lightly in the morning if the air in your home is dry.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 283, 'Give an air plant a soak in a bowl of water for half an hour, then let it dry upside down.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 284, 'Shake old water out of a bromeliad''s central cup and refill it with fresh water.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 285, 'Water an orchid by running water through its bark for a few seconds, then letting it drain completely.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 286, 'Leave an orchid''s green flower spike on after the blooms fall, since it may bloom again.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 287, 'Set an African violet on a saucer and water from below, keeping water off its fuzzy leaves.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 288, 'Remove a spent flower stalk from a peace lily by cutting it low near the base.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 289, 'Snip off brown leaf tips from a spider plant with clean scissors, following the leaf''s natural shape.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 290, 'Take a plant you''ve had for a while out of its spot, look at it in good light, and put it back thoughtfully.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 291, 'Name one of your plants, if you like, and say hello when you check its soil.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 292, 'Silence your phone for ten minutes while you tend your plants, and give them your full attention.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 293, 'Look for a free plant on a neighborhood swap group or free shelf, and give it a good home.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 294, 'Keep a free or hand-me-down plant apart from your others for a couple of weeks, checking it for pests.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 295, 'Take cuttings of a friend''s favorite plant during a visit, with their blessing, and root them at home.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 296, 'Share a few saved seeds with a coworker in a small envelope you decorate.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 297, 'Leave a jar of rooted cuttings in your building''s lobby with a "free" sign, if building rules allow it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 298, 'Host a small plant swap with two or three friends, each bringing a cutting or a pot.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 299, 'Call a relative who gardens and ask them what plant they grew first.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 300, 'Ask an older neighbor how they keep their roses or tomatoes so healthy, and listen closely.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 301, 'Join a local garden club meeting or an online gardening group based in your region.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 302, 'Read one chapter or article on a plant you''re growing, from a library book or an extension guide.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 303, 'Borrow a gardening book from the library and read the section on your favorite plant.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 304, 'Watch a short video from your state''s extension service on a skill like pruning or propagating.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 305, 'Grow cherry tomatoes in a large container in a sunny spot on a balcony or by a south-facing window.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 306, 'Plant a small pot of strawberries in a sunny spot and pinch off runners to keep the plant focused on fruit.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 307, 'Grow a pot of chamomile in a sunny window and brew a cup from its dried flowers.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 308, 'Plant a pot of lavender in full sun with gritty, fast-draining mix, and water only when it is dry.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 309, 'Grow nasturtiums in a pot or bed, and taste one of the peppery flowers you grew yourself.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 310, 'Sow a few radish seeds in a deep pot and pull the roots once their shoulders push up out of the soil.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 311, 'Thin carrot seedlings to two inches apart so each one has room to grow a root.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 312, 'Fill an indoor window planter with herbs like thyme, chives and parsley, using fresh potting mix.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 313, 'Set a long, narrow planter of herbs on a wide indoor sill, with a tray beneath it to catch drips.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 314, 'Put a tray under every indoor pot, so watering doesn''t mark your sill or floor.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 315, 'Water a plant with the cooled, unsalted water left from steaming vegetables.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 316, 'Collect rainwater in a clean covered bucket outdoors and use it on your plants within a week.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 317, 'Catch the cold water from your shower as it warms up, and use it on your houseplants.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 318, 'Pour water slowly around the whole surface of a pot''s soil, not only in one spot near the stem.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 319, 'Keep watering until a little runs from the drainage hole, so the whole root ball gets a drink.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 320, 'Heft a pot before you water it, and notice how much lighter it feels once it has dried out.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 321, 'Push a wooden chopstick into a pot''s soil, pull it out, and see if damp soil clings before you water.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 322, 'Revive a very dry, shrunken pot by soaking it in a sink of water until bubbles stop rising.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 323, 'Let an overwatered plant dry out, moving it to brighter light and pausing the watering for a while.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 324, 'Check the roots of a drooping plant for mushy, dark spots, and trim them with clean scissors before repotting.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 325, 'Let the top inch of soil dry out between waterings if fungus gnats are hovering over a pot.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 326, 'Stick a yellow sticky card in a pot if fungus gnats are buzzing, keeping it out of reach of pets.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 327, 'Look for fine webbing under leaves, a sign of spider mites, and rinse the plant well in the shower.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 328, 'Dab a cotton swab in soapy water and wipe away a cottony white mealybug from a stem.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 329, 'Isolate a plant with pests in another room until it is clean, so the bugs don''t spread.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 330, 'Give a plant a lukewarm shower in the tub to rinse dust and pests from its leaves.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 331, 'Spot a new shoot on a plant today and give yourself a quiet moment to enjoy it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 332, 'Smell a flower on a plant you''ve grown or one in a nearby yard, bending close to breathe it in.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 333, 'Take your morning coffee or tea to wherever your plants are and drink it among them.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 334, 'Put a plant where you can see it from the spot you sit most often.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 335, 'Keep a small plant on your bedside table, choosing one that does fine in low light.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 336, 'Grow a pothos in a jar of water with no soil, topping up and changing the water every week or so.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 337, 'Train a pothos vine along a shelf with small clear hooks so it frames the space.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 338, 'Prop a cutting from a jade plant in dry mix and wait for roots before watering it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 339, 'Grow an aloe plant in a sunny spot, and keep it out of reach of pets, since it can make them sick.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 340, 'Remove a pup from the base of an aloe or a haworthia and pot it on its own.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 341, 'Count the baby plantlets on a spider plant and decide which one you''ll share.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 342, 'Peg a strawberry runner or a spider plant baby into a small pot of soil while it is still attached.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 343, 'Snip the runner once the pegged baby has rooted and can stand on its own.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 344, 'Gather a few leaves for a salad from a container of mixed greens you grew.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 345, 'Cook a simple meal using one ingredient you grew, even just a pinch of herbs.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 346, 'Make pesto from a big basil harvest, and freeze some in an ice cube tray for winter.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 347, 'Freeze chopped herbs in olive oil in an ice cube tray to enjoy your harvest later.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 348, 'Hang a few hot peppers you grew on a string to dry in a warm, airy kitchen.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 349, 'Sketch a seedpod, a bulb or a seed in your journal, drawing it twice its real size.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 350, 'Draw a tiny map of your growing spots, from windowsills to plots, and mark what grows where.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 351, 'Write down the plants you would choose if you had one more pot, and why.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 352, 'Make a list of your plants with the date you got each one, in the back of your journal.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 353, 'Notice a plant in a neighbor''s yard you admire, and tell them or leave a friendly note.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 354, 'Pick up litter around a street tree pit or a public planter on your block, wearing gloves.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 355, 'Water a newly planted street tree near your home during a dry summer spell, if your city welcomes it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 356, 'Learn the name of the street tree outside your home or workplace.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 357, 'Find a plant that blooms in your area in each season, and note them in your journal.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 358, 'Plant a pollinator-friendly herb such as oregano or thyme, and let a few stems flower.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 359, 'Grow a pot of milkweed native to your region, if monarch butterflies pass through.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 360, 'Avoid chemical sprays on your plants, using only plain water or mild soap and water for pests.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 361, 'Tidy your plant shelf: wipe the surface, empty saucers, and stand the pots back in good light.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 362, 'Stand back and look at all your plants together, and notice how your space feels with them in it.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 363, 'Thank someone who helped you grow something, a neighbor, a librarian or a friend who gave a cutting.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 364, 'Think back over this challenge and write down the plant that surprised you most.'),
  ('growing-something-green', 365, 'Choose one new plant or seed to try next, and write where in your space it will grow.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 1, 'Standing in the next checkout line, let your shoulders drop and count five slow breaths before you reach for your phone.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 2, 'Notice where waiting shows up in your body today: a tapping foot, a tight jaw, a held breath. Just name it.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 3, 'When the microwave starts its countdown, stay with it and breathe slowly until it beeps, without opening another app.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 4, 'Next time you are put on hold, switch to speakerphone and wipe down one counter while the music plays.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 5, 'At a red light today, keep your eyes on the road, loosen your grip on the wheel and let one long breath out.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 6, 'Bring a paperback in your bag today so the next wait has something good in it.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 7, 'While a web page loads, unclench your jaw and let your tongue rest at the bottom of your mouth.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 8, 'Say quietly to yourself during the next delay: "This is a small wait, and it will end."'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 9, 'In a waiting room today, find three things you have not noticed before: a picture, a plant, a sound.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 10, 'Thank the cashier by name if they wear a name tag, and notice how the line felt a little shorter.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 11, 'Before a drive with likely traffic, choose a calm playlist while still parked so it is ready to play.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 12, 'When the elevator is slow to arrive, press the button once, step back and feel your feet on the floor.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 13, 'Waiting for the kettle this morning? Stand with it and watch the steam begin instead of leaving the room.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 14, 'If someone behind you has only one or two items, offer to let them go ahead of you.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 15, 'Pick the shortest-looking checkout lane, then let go of checking whether the other lane is moving faster.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 16, 'At the pharmacy counter, take one slow breath in through your nose and a longer one out while you wait for your name.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 17, 'When your bus or train is late, look up from the schedule board and watch the sky for one full minute.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 18, 'Leave five minutes earlier for one errand today so a line there does not set your clock racing.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 19, 'Pack a small snack before you head out, since waiting while hungry makes every minute feel longer.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 20, 'While you wait for a text reply, put the phone face down and do one small task in the room.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 21, 'Notice the moment a wait ends today, and pause for a second to register that it is over.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 22, 'Lift onto your toes and lower down slowly five times while you stand in line, to stretch your calves.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 23, 'Hum a favorite tune under your breath while you wait for the coffee to finish brewing.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 24, 'Imagine the day the person behind the counter has had so far, and offer them a warm word.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 25, 'Waiting at a restaurant for a table? Look around and notice what other people are celebrating.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 26, 'During a long download, step away from the screen and refill your water glass.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 27, 'Keep a short list of three pleasant things to think about during a wait, like a trip you want to plan.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 28, 'Match the pace of a slow walker ahead of you on the sidewalk for ten steps before you pass them kindly.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 29, 'At airport security, take your shoes off slowly and breathe out each time the line moves forward.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 30, 'If your flight is delayed, find a window and watch the ground crew work for five minutes.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 31, 'Waiting for kids to get ready? Sit on the stairs and take three easy breaths instead of calling up again.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 32, 'While on hold with a company, write down the one thing you need from the call so you feel ready when someone answers.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 33, 'Check whether your breath gets shorter when a line stops moving, and lengthen the next out-breath on purpose.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 34, 'Sitting at the DMV, bring a crossword or a word puzzle to fill the time between numbers.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 35, 'When a package is running late, look at the tracking once today and then let it be until tomorrow.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 36, 'In a parking lot exit line, keep your hands soft on the wheel and breathe slowly as the cars ahead move.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 37, 'Spend one minute of your next wait without your phone, just looking around and letting your mind wander.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 38, 'Stand tall in the next line and roll your shoulders back three times, slowly.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 39, 'Waiting for the shower to warm up, feel the steam on your hands and take two slow breaths.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 40, 'Look for a kind detail about a stranger in line: a nice coat, a laughing child, a careful way of bagging groceries.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 41, 'When the toaster is going, rest both hands on the counter and feel its cool surface.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 42, 'Place a book of short poems in the car and read one only while parked and waiting for someone.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 43, 'Write a grocery list during your next hold call so the time does a job for you.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 44, 'When the dentist''s office runs behind, ask the front desk roughly how long it might be, then settle in.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 45, 'Choose a calm phrase for waits, like "Nothing to fix right now," and use it once today.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 46, 'Catch a clenched hand during the next wait and open your fingers one at a time.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 47, 'While a video buffers, look away from the screen toward the farthest point you can see.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 48, 'At a long red light, keep your eyes on the road and say to yourself, "I will get there."'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 49, 'When an email reply is slow to arrive, close the inbox for an hour and work on something else.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 50, 'Waiting for results or news today? Write one kind sentence to yourself on a sticky note and keep it close.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 51, 'Mail your package at a quieter hour, like mid-morning, so the post office line is easier to stand in.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 52, 'In a holiday shopping line, notice the decorations around you and pick out the one you like best.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 53, 'Let the driver who reached the four-way stop at the same time as you go first, with a small wave.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 54, 'Waiting for the weekend to arrive? Plan one small pleasure for Saturday morning and write it down.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 55, 'Ask yourself during the next delay, "Will this wait matter tonight?" and let the answer settle you.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 56, 'On a late train platform, lean against a wall or pillar and feel it holding you up.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 57, 'Soften your forehead and the space between your eyebrows the next time a screen freezes.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 58, 'Carry a small notebook today and jot one thought down during each wait.'),
  ('finding-patience-in-everyday-waiting', 59, 'Offer a smile to the person who finally calls your name in the waiting room.'),
